<title>UK: Brent Walker to announce Pubmaster sale - FT.</title>
<headline>Brent Walker to announce Pubmaster sale - FT.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Debt-laden leisure group Brent Walker Plc is poised to announce on Thursday the sale of its Pubmaster pub chain, the Financial Times reported.</p>
<p>The buyer is understood to be NatWest, which is leading a syndicate of other venture capitalists. The price of the 1,700 strong chain is expected to be between 160 million and 170 million stg, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Brent Walker announced in October the selection of a preferred bidder for Pubmaster, but had not named the chosen candidate.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7717</p>
